msgstr "HABIT 的稳定异常契约。"
#: ../../../habit/exceptions.py:docstring of habit.exceptions:3
msgid "This module is the canonical home of HABIT's exception hierarchy. It sits at the foundation of the layering rules: it must never import other ``habit`` modules, so every layer (kernels -> contracts -> domain -> api -> interfaces) can depend on it without creating import cycles."
msgstr ""
"本模块是 HABIT 异常层次结构的规范归属。它位于分层规则的基础：不得 import 其他 ``habit`` 模块，以便各层（kernels -> contracts -> domain -> api -> interfaces）可依赖它而不形成 import 环。"
#: ../../../habit/exceptions.py:docstring of habit.exceptions:8
msgid "The canonical definitions live in this module. New code should import from here."
msgstr "规范定义位于本模块。新代码应从此处导入。"
#: ../../../habit/exceptions.py:docstring of habit.exceptions:11
msgid "``NotFittedError`` is constructed lazily via PEP 562 ``__getattr__``: it must subclass :class:`sklearn.exceptions.NotFittedError` for sklearn interop, but importing sklearn at module scope would drag the entire scientific-Python stack into every bare ``import habit`` (this module sits on the foundation import path). The sklearn import therefore happens only on first access of the class; ``import habit`` itself stays sklearn-free."
msgstr ""
"``NotFittedError`` 通过 PEP 562 ``__getattr__`` 惰性构造：为与 sklearn 互操作须子类化 :class:`sklearn.exceptions.NotFittedError` ，但在模块作用域导入 sklearn 会使每次裸 ``import habit`` 拖入整个科学 Python 栈（本模块位于基础导入路径）。因此 sklearn 仅在首次访问该类时导入； ``import habit`` 本身不依赖 sklearn。"
