#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:470
msgid "The ML recipes are v1-native: :func:`~habit.recipes.train_model`, :func:`~habit.recipes.cross_validate`, and :func:`~habit.recipes.predict_model` take a :class:`~habit.contracts.FeatureTable` plus an :class:`~habit.spec.specs.MLSpec` and run a :class:`~habit.pipeline.TablePipeline` — fitted preprocessing and selection state travels inside the saved pipeline, so prediction never refits on new data. Tabular building blocks are documented in :doc:`domain_table`."
msgstr "ML recipes 为 v1 原生： :func:`~habit.recipes.train_model` 、 :func:`~habit.recipes.cross_validate` 、 :func:`~habit.recipes.predict_model` 接受 :class:`~habit.contracts.FeatureTable` 与 :class:`~habit.spec.specs.MLSpec` ，运行 :class:`~habit.pipeline.TablePipeline` ——拟合的预处理与选择状态保存在 pipeline 内，预测时不会在新数据上重拟合。表格构建块见 :doc:`domain_table` 。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:502
msgid "``make_synthetic_feature_table`` is built for golden tests (one strong ``signal`` column) and will often print AUC 1.0. For publication-style figures see :doc:`/auto_examples/04_quantifying_habitats/plot_01_volume_fractions`."
msgstr ""
"``make_synthetic_feature_table`` is built for golden tests (one strong ``signal`` column) and will often print AUC 1.0. For publication-style figures see :doc:`/auto_examples/04_quantifying_habitats/plot_01_volume_fractions`."
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:506
msgid "Steps interleave freely, which the three predecessor fields could not express. ``zscore`` → ``variance`` → ``minmax`` → ``lasso`` is a plain list:"
msgstr ""
"步骤可自由交错，三个前身字段无法表达。 ``zscore`` → ``variance`` → ``minmax`` → ``lasso`` 即普通列表："
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:522
msgid "The fields ``pre_preprocessing_feature_selectors``, ``table_preprocessors`` and ``feature_selectors`` are deprecated aliases kept for all of v1.x. They are folded into ``steps`` in that documented order and raise a ``DeprecationWarning``; a spec declaring both layouts with different content is rejected rather than resolved by precedence."
msgstr ""
"字段 ``pre_preprocessing_feature_selectors`` 、 ``table_preprocessors`` 、 ``feature_selectors`` 为 v1.x 全程保留的弃用别名，按文档顺序并入 ``steps`` 并发出 ``DeprecationWarning`` ；同时声明两种布局且内容不同时拒绝而非按优先级解析。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:529
msgid "Hyperparameter search and nested cross-validation"
msgstr "超参数搜索与嵌套交叉验证"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:531
msgid ":func:`~habit.recipes.search_hyperparameters` tunes a spec with scikit-learn's ``GridSearchCV`` / ``RandomizedSearchCV`` and writes the winners **back into the** :class:`~habit.spec.specs.MLSpec`. That is the point of the recipe: a tuned model is a *definition*, so it keeps a fingerprint, serialises to YAML and can be re-run by a reader — a search that returned only a fitted object would end the provenance chain where the parameters were chosen."
msgstr ""
":func:`~habit.recipes.search_hyperparameters` 用 scikit-learn 的 ``GridSearchCV`` / ``RandomizedSearchCV`` 调参，并将优胜者 **写回** :class:`~habit.spec.specs.MLSpec` 。这正是该配方的要点：调优后的模型是一种 *定义* ，因此保留指纹、可序列化到 YAML、读者可重跑——若搜索只返回拟合对象，溯源链会在参数选定处断裂。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:538
msgid "Grid keys address one HABIT component parameter through the pipeline's step names, ``\"<step>__component__<parameter>\"``. The terminal model's step is ``\"model\"``; every other step is named after its registered spec name:"
msgstr ""
"Grid keys address one HABIT component parameter through the pipeline's step names, ``\"<step>__component__<parameter>\"``. The terminal model's step is ``\"model\"``; every other step is named after its registered spec name:"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:559
msgid "The folds come from :func:`habit.evaluation.split.kfold_indices`, so a search partitions the rows exactly as :func:`~habit.recipes.cross_validate` does for the same ``n_splits`` and seed, and every candidate is fitted on training rows only — preprocessing statistics and feature selection included, because they are pipeline steps that get cloned per fold. ``strategy=\"random\"`` switches to a sampled search with an ``n_iter`` budget. The objective's own ``greater_is_better`` sets the direction, so a \"lower is better\" metric is minimised without the caller negating anything; omitted, the objective is the first metric of ``spec.metrics``, and ``auc`` for a spec with no panel."
msgstr ""
"折划分来自 :func:`habit.evaluation.split.kfold_indices` ，搜索与相同 ``n_splits`` 和 seed 下 :func:`~habit.recipes.cross_validate` 完全一致，且每个候选仅在训练行上拟合——含预处理统计与特征选择，因它们是每折克隆的 pipeline 步骤。 ``strategy=\"random\"`` 切换为带 ``n_iter`` 预算的采样搜索。目标自身的 ``greater_is_better`` 决定方向，故“越小越好”的指标无需调用方取负；省略时目标为 ``spec.metrics`` 的第一项，无面板时用 ``auc`` 。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:569
msgid "Tuning once on all the rows and cross-validating afterwards reports an optimistically biased number, because the validation rows took part in the selection. Passing ``inner_cv`` together with ``param_grid`` makes :func:`~habit.recipes.cross_validate` nested instead: each outer fold re-tunes on its own training rows and is scored on rows neither the tuning nor the fit has seen."
msgstr ""
"先在全部行上调参再交叉验证会得到偏乐观的数字，因为验证行参与了选择。同时传入 ``inner_cv`` 与 ``param_grid`` 使 :func:`~habit.recipes.cross_validate` 变为嵌套：每个外层折在自己的训练行上重调参，并在调参与拟合都未见过的行上评分。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:589
msgid "Report ``fold_best_params`` alongside the panel: parameters that change from fold to fold say the search is fitting noise. The two arguments are required together — a grid without ``inner_cv`` has nowhere to tune except the outer validation rows, and ``inner_cv`` without a grid searches over nothing. There is deliberately no Bayesian/Optuna backend, which would be a new hard dependency."
msgstr ""
"将 ``fold_best_params`` 与面板一起报告：那些在每折中变化的参数表明搜索正在拟合噪声。这两个参数必须一起使用——没有 ``inner_cv`` 的网格除了外部验证行之外无处调优，而没有网格的 ``inner_cv`` 则无法进行任何搜索。故意没有 Bayesian/Optuna 后端，因为那将成为新的硬依赖。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:596
msgid "CLI users keep ``habit get-habitat -c ...``; that path translates YAML through ``LegacyConfigAdapter`` / ``HabitatSpec`` into the same domain core, and :func:`~habit.recipes.run_from_yaml` exposes the identical path to Python callers (see :ref:`the YAML section <common-workflows-yaml>` above)."
msgstr "CLI 用户仍用 ``habit get-habitat -c ...`` ；该路径经 ``LegacyConfigAdapter`` / ``HabitatSpec`` 将 YAML 译为同一领域核心， :func:`~habit.recipes.run_from_yaml` 向 Python 调用者暴露相同路径（见上文 :ref:`YAML 小节 <common-workflows-yaml>` ）。"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:602
msgid "Feature extraction (config-driven)"
msgstr "特征提取（配置驱动）"
#: ../../source/api/python_api.rst:604
msgid "``habit.recipes.extract_habitat_features`` and ``habit.recipes.traditional_radiomics`` exist so ``habit extract`` and ``habit radiomics`` can route through L4 recipes. They are **not** the recommended Python path: no domain-native cohort assembly, no ``SubjectPipeline`` / ``TablePipeline``, and no ``StudyResult`` contract. For habitat features in library code, prefer :class:`~habit.pipeline.SubjectPipeline` ``.extract_features(...)`` with the ``habitat_feature_extractor`` registry (:doc:`domain_habitat`)."
msgstr ""
"``habit.recipes.extract_habitat_features`` and ``habit.recipes.traditional_radiomics`` exist so ``habit extract`` and ``habit radiomics`` can route through L4 recipes. They are **not** the recommended Python path: no domain-native 队列 assembly, no ``SubjectPipeline`` / ``TablePipeline``, and no ``StudyResult`` contract. For 生境 特征 in library code, prefer :class:`~habit.pipeline.SubjectPipeline` ``.extract_features(...)`` with the ``habitat_feature_extractor`` registry (:doc:`domain_habitat`)."
#: ../../source/api/recipes.rst:4
msgid ":mod:`habit.recipes`: named study designs"
msgstr ":mod:`habit.recipes` ：命名研究设计"
#: ../../../habit/recipes/__init__.py:docstring of habit.recipes:1
msgid "L4 recipes: named study designs, assembled from L3 components."
msgstr "L4 配方：命名研究设计，由 L3 组件装配。"
#: ../../../habit/recipes/__init__.py:docstring of habit.recipes:3
msgid "A recipe is the shortest path from \"I want a two-step habitat analysis\" to a result object, and nothing more. It contains no engine of its own: no run loop, no resume, no configuration parsing, no output directory. Those live in the execution backends (L1/L2), the writers (L1) and the CLI (L5) respectively, which is what keeps a recipe callable from a notebook, a web service or someone else's pipeline."
msgstr ""
"recipe 是从“我要两步法生境分析”到结果对象的最短路径，仅此而已。它不含自有引擎：无运行循环、无恢复、无配置解析、无输出目录。这些分别在执行后端（L1/L2）、写入器（L1）与 CLI（L5），因此 recipe 可在 notebook、Web 服务或他人流水线中调用。"
#: ../../source/api/recipes.rst:13
msgid "**User guide:** Habitat Guide :doc:`../auto_examples/index` (especially :doc:`../auto_examples/00_introductory_tutorials/index`) · :doc:`python_api`. Component names: :doc:`../how_to/habitat_components`."
msgstr "**用户指南：** 生境指南 :doc:`../auto_examples/index` （尤其 :doc:`../auto_examples/00_introductory_tutorials/index` ）· :doc:`python_api` 。组件名： :doc:`../how_to/habitat_components` 。"
#: ../../source/api/recipes.rst:18
msgid "Primary entry: :class:`~habit.recipes.Study` (sklearn-style :meth:`~habit.recipes.Study.fit` / :meth:`~habit.recipes.Study.fit_predict` / :meth:`~habit.recipes.Study.predict`). Factories ``two_step_habitat`` / ``one_step_habitat`` / ``direct_pooling_habitat`` build a :class:`~habit.recipes.Study` with a declared design."
msgstr "主入口： :class:`~habit.recipes.Study` （sklearn 风格 :meth:`~habit.recipes.Study.fit` / :meth:`~habit.recipes.Study.fit_predict` / :meth:`~habit.recipes.Study.predict` ）。工厂 ``two_step_habitat`` / ``one_step_habitat`` / ``direct_pooling_habitat`` 构建带声明设计的 :class:`~habit.recipes.Study` 。"
