#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:12
msgid "Habitat overlays use ``ImageVolume`` + ``HabitatMap`` (not raw arrays and not ``direction=``). Same colour means the same habitat id when a cohort model was fitted."
msgstr ""
"生境叠加使用 ``ImageVolume`` + ``HabitatMap`` （非原始数组且非 ``direction=`` ）。拟合队列模型时同色即同一生境 id。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:17
msgid "Choosing the number of habitats"
msgstr "选择生境数量"
#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:19
msgid "When ``n_habitats`` is omitted, k-means tries every candidate in ``min_habitats`` … ``max_habitats`` and keeps the count preferred by ``validation`` (schema default ``elbow``). Report the rule and the random seed with the results."
msgstr "省略 ``n_habitats`` 时，k-means 会尝试 ``min_habitats`` … ``max_habitats`` 中的每一个候选，并保留 ``validation`` 所偏好的个数（schema 默认 ``elbow`` ）。报告结果时请同时写明选用规则与随机种子。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:24
msgid "HABIT validation ``elbow`` is the same rule as ``kneedle``. It runs ``KneeLocator`` on k-means inertia (within-cluster sum of squares), curve convex, direction decreasing (Satopaa, Albrecht, Irwin, and Raghavan, 2011, *Finding a \"Kneedle\" in a Haystack*, IEEE ICDCS Workshops). In two sentences: normalize ``k`` and inertia to the unit square, draw the chord from the first point to the last, and take the ``k`` farthest from that chord. A smooth curve often places this knee to the right of the bend a person sees."
msgstr ""
"HABIT 验证 ``elbow`` 与 ``kneedle`` 为同一规则。在 k-means 惯性（簇内平方和）上运行 ``KneeLocator`` ，曲线 convex、方向 decreasing（Satopaa, Albrecht, Irwin, and Raghavan, 2011, *Finding a \"Kneedle\" in a Haystack*, IEEE ICDCS Workshops）。简述：将 ``k`` 与 inertia 归一化到单位正方形，连接首尾点作弦，取离弦最远的 ``k`` ；平滑曲线常使该 knee 位于肉眼弯折点右侧。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:33
msgid "In the clustering literature, *elbow* usually means looking at within-cluster dispersion versus ``k`` and choosing where extra clusters stop helping (Thorndike RL, 1953, *Who belongs in the family?*, Psychometrika 18(4):267–276, as that early statement). Do **not** claim Thorndike published a second-difference formula."
msgstr "在聚类文献中， *elbow* 通常指观察簇内离散度随 ``k`` 的变化，并选择额外簇不再有帮助的拐点（Thorndike RL, 1953, *Who belongs in the family?*, Psychometrika 18(4):267–276，即该早期表述）。 **不要** 声称 Thorndike 发表过二阶差分公式。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:39
msgid "HABIT also documents a **discrete-curvature elbow** (visual elbow, computed): the ``k`` that maximizes the second difference of inertia (``argmax(diff2) + 1`` into the candidate list). That was the rule HABIT used for ``elbow`` before v1.0. Label it *discrete-curvature elbow*, not “Thorndike formula”."
msgstr ""
"HABIT 亦文档化 **离散曲率肘部** （视觉肘部、可计算）：最大化 inertia 二阶差的 ``k`` （ ``argmax(diff2) + 1`` 进入候选列表）。这是 HABIT 在 v1.0 前 ``elbow`` 用的规则。标注为 *离散曲率肘部* ，非「Thorndike 公式」。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/building_habitat_maps.rst:45
msgid "Other k-means criteria in :mod:`habit.kernels.cluster_selection` — maximize: ``silhouette``, ``calinski_harabasz``, ``gap``; minimize: ``davies_bouldin``; knee: ``elbow`` / ``kneedle`` / ``inertia``. GMM also supports minimize ``bic`` / ``aic`` and ``bic_elbow`` (Prior 2024 BIC-slope rule). Criteria disagree on the same curve; the gallery page :doc:`/auto_examples/03_clustering/plot_03_clustering_algorithm` prints a comparison table and marks both the Kneedle ``k`` and the discrete-curvature ``k`` on the inertia panel."
msgstr ""
":mod:`habit.kernels.cluster_selection` 中其他 k-means 准则 — 最大化： ``silhouette`` 、 ``calinski_harabasz`` 、 ``gap`` ；最小化： ``davies_bouldin`` ；拐点： ``elbow`` / ``kneedle`` / ``inertia`` 。GMM 还支持最小化 ``bic`` / ``aic`` 与 ``bic_elbow`` （Prior 2024 BIC 斜率规则）。同一曲线上准则可不一致；图库页 :doc:`/auto_examples/03_clustering/plot_03_clustering_algorithm` 打印对照表并在 inertia 面板标 Kneedle ``k`` 与离散曲率 ``k`` 。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/features.rst:4
msgid "Voxel features are the columns clustering sees: multi-sequence intensities, texture families on one sequence, enhancement patterns (ratio, difference, average, expression, kinetic), and concatenated routes. See Examples → Features."
msgstr ""
"体素特征为聚类所见列：多序列强度、单序列纹理族、增强模式（ratio、difference、average、expression、kinetic）及拼接路径。见 Examples → Features。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:4
msgid "**habitat** — sub-region of the ROI with similar voxel features."
msgstr "**habitat** —— ROI 内体素特征相似的子区域。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:5
msgid "**ROI / mask** — region analysed; background is 0."
msgstr "**ROI / 掩膜** — 分析区域；背景为 0。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:6
msgid "**subject-level preprocessing** — transform using one patient's statistics only (default: winsorize 1% + z-score)."
msgstr ""
"**受试者级预处理** — transform using one 患者's statistics only (default: winsorize 1% + z-score)."
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:8
msgid "**cohort-level preprocessing** — transform learned on pooled training rows and stored in the model (not the default after subject z-score)."
msgstr ""
"**cohort-level preprocessing** —— 在池化训练行上学习并存入模型的变换（非受试者 z-score 后的默认）。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:10
msgid "**supervoxel** — small patch of similar neighbouring voxels."
msgstr "**超体素** — 相似邻近体素小 patch。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:11
msgid "**pool** — stack per-subject units into one matrix."
msgstr "**pool** — 将逐受试者单元堆成一张矩阵。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/glossary.rst:12
msgid "**.habitatmodel** — saved habitat definition for reuse."
msgstr "**.habitatmodel** —— 可复用的已保存生境定义。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/index.rst:4
msgid "Narrative overview of habitat analysis with HABIT. Examples carry the full code; this guide explains *what* and *why*, and links out."
msgstr "HABIT 生境分析叙述概览。示例含完整代码；本指南解释 *什么* 与 *为何* 并外链。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:2
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "引言"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:5
msgid "What habitat analysis asks"
msgstr "生境分析在问什么"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:7
msgid "A whole-tumour summary collapses the ROI into one average. Inside many lesions, subregions enhance, necrose, or sit in different locations. **Habitat analysis** partitions the ROI into a few spatially coherent subregions (**habitats**) whose voxels behave alike across the input images, then describes each patient by how much of each habitat they have and how those habitats are arranged in space."
msgstr "全肿瘤汇总会把 ROI 压成一个平均值。许多病灶内部，子区域会强化、坏死，或处于不同位置。 **生境分析** 将 ROI 划分为若干空间上连贯的子区域（ **生境** ），其体素在输入图像上表现相近，再以各生境所占比例及其空间排布来描述每一位患者。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:15
msgid "Practical challenges"
msgstr "实践挑战"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:17
msgid "Doing this well—and so that a second lab can rerun it—is harder than drawing a mask and clustering once."
msgstr "做好且让第二实验室可复跑，比画掩膜聚类一次更难。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:20
msgid "A whole-tumour feature table hides those subregions; two patients can share a similar average and still differ where habitats sit."
msgstr "全肿瘤特征表隐藏那些子区域；两患者平均相似仍可在生境位置上不同。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:22
msgid "Published pipelines disagree on design: cluster inside each patient, pool voxels across the cohort, or build supervoxels then fit a cohort model. Results are hard to compare or reproduce when the design is not named clearly."
msgstr "已发表流水线在设计上分歧：各患者内聚类、跨队列池化体素，或建超体素再拟合队列模型。设计未清晰命名时结果难以比较或复现。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:26
msgid "MRI signal is not a quantitative unit across patients and scans. A model fit on raw intensities can paint a new patient as a single habitat. Intensities need subject-level scaling before cross-patient clustering; the concrete step is in Examples and :doc:`building_habitat_maps`."
msgstr ""
"MRI 信号在患者与扫描间非定量单位。在原始强度上拟合的模型可能把新患者画成单一生境。跨患者聚类前须受试者级缩放；具体步骤见 Examples 与 :doc:`building_habitat_maps` 。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:31
msgid "Habitat IDs swap between fits, so colours and column names do not match until labels are aligned."
msgstr "生境 ID 在拟合间会互换，颜色与列名在对齐前不一致。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:33
msgid "A saved model applied to a new cohort is wrong if the feature space differs, and the failure can look like a plausible map."
msgstr "保存模型用于新队列时，若特征空间不同则错误，失败可像合理图。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:35
msgid "Readers need a path from images to habitat maps, to numbers (volume, spatial interaction, heterogeneity, graph layout), and to a methods paragraph they can put in a paper."
msgstr "读者需要从图像到生境图，再到数值（体积、空间相互作用、异质性、图布局），再到可写入论文的方法段。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:40
msgid "What HABIT is for"
msgstr "HABIT 的用途"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:42
msgid "HABIT is a Python library for that path. The Python API is the product: the same analysis can be declared as a ``HabitatSpec``, assembled from atomic components, or driven by a short YAML / CLI recipe."
msgstr ""
"HABIT 是沿该路径的 Python 库。Python API 即产品：同一分析可声明为 ``HabitatSpec`` 、由原子组件组装，或由短 YAML / CLI 配方驱动。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:46
msgid "Three habitat designs share one vocabulary: **two-step** (supervoxels, then a cohort model), **inside each subject**, and **pooled voxels**."
msgstr "三种生境设计共用词汇： **两步法** （超体素再队列模型）、 **受试者内** 、 **池化体素** 。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:49
msgid "You can embed it: arrays in, habitat map out, without HABIT's folder layout."
msgstr "可嵌入使用：数组进、生境图出，无需 HABIT 目录布局。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:51
msgid "Fit once, save a ``HabitatModel``, and apply it to new patients."
msgstr "拟合一次，保存 ``HabitatModel`` ，并应用于新患者。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:52
msgid "Quantify habitats: volume fractions, MSI, ITH, per-habitat and whole-map radiomics, and graph-network features that describe how habitats sit in space."
msgstr "量化生境：体积分数、MSI、ITH、逐生境与全图放射组学，及描述生境空间关系的图网络特征。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:55
msgid "Radiomics on habitat maps follow IBSI / PyRadiomics definitions, with an IBSI-1 Phase 1 digital-phantom comparison on :doc:`/reference/features/traditional`."
msgstr ""
"生境图上的放射组学遵循 IBSI / PyRadiomics 定义，并在 :doc:`/reference/features/traditional` 提供 IBSI-1 Phase 1 数字体膜对照。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:58
msgid "Screen features for reproducibility (**precise features**) and match habitat labels across fits."
msgstr "筛选可复现特征（ **precise features** ）并在多次拟合间匹配生境标签。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:60
msgid "Run a cohort with a simple serial backend; scale with a process backend, failure policy, and resume when the cohort is large."
msgstr "用简单串行后端跑队列；队列较大时改用进程后端、失败策略与断点续跑扩展。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:62
msgid "``describe_methods()`` drafts the methods paragraph from the run itself."
msgstr "``describe_methods()`` 从运行本身起草方法段落。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:66
msgid "How to use this documentation"
msgstr "如何使用本文档"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:68
msgid "**Quickstart** — :doc:`/auto_quickstart/plot_quickstart_python` (YAML twin: :doc:`/auto_quickstart/plot_quickstart_yaml`)."
msgstr "**快速开始** —— :doc:`/auto_quickstart/plot_quickstart_python` （YAML 对应： :doc:`/auto_quickstart/plot_quickstart_yaml` ）。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:70
msgid "**Examples** — end-to-end code under :doc:`/auto_examples/index`, starting with the introductory tutorials."
msgstr "**示例** — :doc:`/auto_examples/index` 下的端到端代码，从入门教程开始。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/introduction.rst:73
msgid "**User guide** — short *what* / *why* pages; copy runnable code from Examples. Next: :doc:`building_habitat_maps`, :doc:`features`, :doc:`quantifying_habitats`."
msgstr "**用户指南** — 简短 *什么*/*为何* 页；从 Examples 复制可运行代码。下一步： :doc:`building_habitat_maps` 、 :doc:`features` 、 :doc:`quantifying_habitats` 。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/manipulating_images.rst:4
msgid "Load a HABIT directory, NIfTI files, SimpleITK images, NumPy arrays, or a user-supplied named mask. See Examples → Manipulating images."
msgstr ""
"加载 HABIT 目录、NIfTI、SimpleITK 图像、NumPy 数组或用户提供的命名掩膜。见 Examples → Manipulating images"
#: ../../source/user_guide/optional_dependencies.rst:2
msgid "Optional dependencies"
msgstr "可选依赖"
#: ../../source/user_guide/optional_dependencies.rst:4
msgid "Install extras only when you need them, for example::"
msgstr "仅在需要时安装 extras，例如::"
#: ../../source/user_guide/optional_dependencies.rst:8
msgid "See :doc:`/tutorial/installation` for the full list (napari / Qt view, GPU texture, registration, AutoML, and so on). Missing optionals raise ``OptionalDependencyError`` with an install hint."
msgstr ""
"完整列表见 :doc:`/tutorial/installation` （napari / Qt view、GPU 纹理、配准、AutoML 等）。缺失可选依赖时抛出 ``OptionalDependencyError`` 并提示安装。"
#: ../../source/user_guide/quantifying_habitats.rst:4
msgid "Volume fractions, MSI, ITH, HABIT graph-network features, and habitat radiomics turn a label map into a patient-level table. MSI metrics that are comparable across patients are called out on the MSI example page."
msgstr "体积分数、MSI、ITH、HABIT 图网络特征与生境放射组学将标签图转为患者级表。可跨患者比较的 MSI 指标在 MSI 示例页标明。"
